  "name": "Driven two-level atom: optical Bloch relaxation",
  "category": "physics",
  "description": "Rotating-frame two-level density matrix in ordered basis(g,e): rho=[[1-p,x+i*y],[x-i*y,p]]. Hamiltonian/hbar=[[-Delta/2,Omega/2],[Omega/2,Delta/2]], collapse operator sqrt(Gamma)*|g><e|. Real coherence x, imaginary coherence y and excited probability p evolve under coherent drive and spontaneous emission. Rotating-wave, weak-coupling Markov/secular approximation; no cavity, propagation, many atoms or extra pure dephasing. Default Gamma1,Omega2,Delta0.5 per second, initially ground; end20 step0.02. Physical initial density matrices require0<=p<=1 and x^2+y^2<=p*(1-p); Gamma>=0. Step selection is numerical, not a positivity repair. Original mathematical transcription/derivation; parameters are illustrative, not empirical calibration. Signed net-rate flows represent derivatives, not nonnegative physical transfers. No clamps or hidden resets.",
  "source": "https://qutip.readthedocs.io/en/stable/guide/dynamics/dynamics-master.html",
  "reference": "QuTiP documentation, Lindblad Master Equation Solver equation3. Original real-component derivation for the explicitly stated Hamiltonian/collapse operator; not copied QuTiP code or a QuTiP execution/parity receipt.",
